            <ArticleTitle>[Text messaging and self-care support of hypertensive patients : first achievements].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1566-1569</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Text messaging applied to self-care support of hypertensive patients is a new e-health tool available via mobile phones and computers. First validated programs are just emerging. Without being a panacea intended to replace the doctors by machines they could be provide a significant reinforcement of the patient's empowerment for self-monitoring. It is now time to begin their evaluation in real life and in primary care setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
